<title>LEBANON: SOLIDERE mixed in Beirut.</title>
<headline>SOLIDERE mixed in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SOLIDERE shares were mixed on Friday on the last day of trade on the privately-operated Beirut Secondary Market (BSM).</p>
<p>The shares will begin trading on the official Beirut Stock Exchange (BSE) on Monday.</p>
<p>A shares rose to $112.5 from $108 on Thursday and B shares fell to $113.0 from $113.625.</p>
<p>The shares had rallied in the previous two weeks amid expectations that SOLIDERE will launch a $150 million GDR issue in October allowing non-Arab investors access to the market.</p>
<p>Turnover on BSM, which trades only SOLIDERE shares, was 5,226 shares from 4,101 on Thursday. Value was $580,192 compared with $442,834.</p>
<p>There was no trade on the BSE in any of the four listed companies: Ciments Libanais, Ciments Blancs, Eternit and Uniceramic.</p>
<p>The LISPI stock index rose 0.15 percent to 83.74 and BLOM stock index rose 3.9 percent to 964.3. They cover both markets.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 353078 861723</p>
